<file path="README.md">
# SOMIPHARM Frontend – Equipment + SerialNumber rewrite

This is the next frontend phase after Stock + Shelf.

## Implemented

### Equipment

- Equipment status is visible and editable:
  - `ACTIVE`
  - `INACTIVE`
- Status can be selected during creation.
- `Standard -> Serialized` conversion is available from Edit.
- `Serialized -> Standard` is not offered.
- If standard physical quantity is `0`, conversion requires no initial serials.
- If physical quantity is greater than `0`, the UI:
  - loads the current allocations,
  - requires one manual serial code per physical unit,
  - preserves the current shelf of every unit,
  - sends backend `conversionSerials`.
- Physical quantity remains read-only in Equipment CRUD.
- Equipment row actions are only:
  - Voir
  - Modifier
  - Supprimer
- Movement button is removed from every equipment row/page/detail.
- Shelf-view button/modal is no longer used by the Equipment page.
- Equipment list has no UUID search/copy/display.

### Equipment "Voir"

The detail modal displays only:

- equipment summary/status,
- serial numbers when serialized,
- movement history.

There is no current-shelves section and no movement creation action.

### SerialNumber

- Serial code is always manually entered.
- No automatic serial code generator exists in this rewrite.
- Serial code is immutable after creation.
- Editing a serial changes `serialNumberStatus` only.
- "Ajouter" in Equipment detail requires the user to type the code.
- Creating/deleting serial identity does not directly edit physical Equipment quantity; backend remains authoritative.

## Files

- `src/app/equipment/page.tsx`
- `src/types/equipment.ts`
- `src/schemas/equipment.schema.ts`
- `src/services/equipment.service.ts`
- `src/services/serial-number.service.ts`
- `src/hooks/use-equipments.ts`
- `src/hooks/use-serial-numbers.ts`
- `src/components/equipment/CreateEquipmentModal.tsx`
